  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening accountability for conflict-related sexual violence crimes in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the full-scale invasion of Ukraine by the Russian Federation on 24 February 2022, there has been evidence and reports of war crimes, crimes against humanity and other serious violations of international humanitarian law and human rights law, including conflict-related sexual violence (CRSV). Cases of CRSV crimes have been documented against women, men, girls and boys, and it is expected that the number of documented cases will continue to grow as the armed conflict continues and more evide</narrative>
  </description>
